# Firebase + App Hosting (ecommerce layer)

Verified 2026-09-28 against the sources in `docs/adr/0007`. Check Context7 or the Firebase docs
before you change a value, and date the change.

## Shape

```
app/(site)/…            storefront, cart, checkout, account — Server Components first
app/admin/…             admin: own layout, noindex
app/api/…               route handlers: cart/validate, cart/discount, orders, search, auth/session, payments/<bank>/…
lib/firebase/admin.ts   firebase-admin — starts with `import "server-only"`
lib/firebase/client.ts  web SDK — Auth in the browser, nothing else writes from the client
lib/shop/               schemas.ts (zod) · money.ts · catalog.ts · orders.ts · settings.ts · auth.ts · cities.ts
lib/images/loader.ts    picks the smallest pre-sized WebP width ≥ the requested one
stores/cart.ts          zustand cart, persisted
emails/                 react-email templates
scripts/                seed.ts · set-admin.ts · verify-catalog.ts
tests/                  unit/ (no emulator) · rules/ and emulator/ (emulator) · e2e/ (Playwright)
firebase.json · .firebaserc · firestore.rules · storage.rules · firestore.indexes.json · apphosting.yaml
```

## SDKs

- Server code uses `firebase-admin` only. Call `initializeApp()` with no arguments: App Hosting
  injects `FIREBASE_CONFIG`; locally the emulator variables point it at the emulators.
- The browser uses the web SDK for sign-in and the ID token only. It never reads or writes Firestore.

## Local development

- Emulators for Auth, Firestore and Storage: `pnpm emulators`. Project id **`demo-<slug>`** — the
  `demo-` prefix never touches a real project. The emulators need **Java JDK 11+** (install 21).
- `pnpm seed` fills the emulator with invented data shaped like the client's catalog. Never real
  customer data. Never the feature reference's catalog.
- `.env.local`: `FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST`, `FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST`,
  `FIREBASE_STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST`, `GCLOUD_PROJECT=demo-<slug>`, and demo `NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_*` values.
- Scripts run with `tsx --conditions=react-server` (then `server-only` is an empty import):
  `pnpm run:local <script>` on the emulator, `pnpm run:remote <script> --project <id>` on a real
  project (the project id, not the `.firebaserc` alias). A remote script refuses to start when an
  `*_EMULATOR_HOST` variable is set. It reads `--project`, sets `process.env.FIREBASE_CONFIG`
  (`projectId`, `storageBucket`), and only then does `await import("@/lib/firebase/admin")`.
  Once per machine and project: `gcloud auth application-default login` and
  `gcloud auth application-default set-quota-project <id>`.

## Rules, indexes, tests

- `firestore.rules` stays **deny-all** for the whole project. `storage.rules` allows `get` (not
  `list`) of `products/**` and `content/**` and no client writes.
- Rules tests use `@firebase/rules-unit-testing` on the emulator (`pnpm test:rules`). For every
  collection, an anonymous and a signed-in client can neither read nor write. A unit that adds a
  collection adds it to the test list in the same PR.
- Tests that need data (orders, admin actions) live in `tests/emulator/` (`pnpm test:emulator`).
  `pnpm test` runs `tests/unit/` only and needs no emulator.
- A query with a filter plus an order needs an entry in `firestore.indexes.json`.
- Deploy rules and indexes: `firebase deploy --only firestore,storage --project <alias>`.

## Next.js on App Hosting

- `next.config.ts`: `output: "standalone"`. No `cacheComponents`. No access control in `proxy.ts`.
- **The build never reads Firestore.** `app/(site)/layout.tsx`, `app/admin/layout.tsx` and
  `app/sitemap.ts` export `const dynamic = "force-dynamic"`. No `generateStaticParams` for shop data.
  The root `app/not-found.tsx` stays static without Firestore; the branded 404 is `app/(site)/not-found.tsx`.
- Uncached queries live in `lib/shop/*-queries.ts`. Pages call cached wrappers:
  `unstable_cache(fn, [key], { revalidate: 300, tags: ["catalog"] })` (settings: tag `settings`;
  home blocks: tag `content`). Admin saves call `updateTag(<tag>)`. Other server instances catch up
  within 5 minutes — tell the client.
- Cached functions return plain JSON: dates as ISO strings, no `Timestamp`, `Date` or class objects.
- Scripts, tests, the cart check, the order route, account and admin pages use the uncached queries.
- Route handlers and server actions: parse input with `zod` → check the session → act.
- Next.js 16: `params`, `searchParams`, `cookies()` and `headers()` are async — `await` them.
  `pnpm lint` runs `eslint .` (`next lint` is gone).

## Sessions

- Client sign-in → ID token → `POST /api/auth/session` → `createSessionCookie` → the cookie
  **`__session`** (httpOnly, secure, sameSite `lax`, 14 days). App Hosting was reported to strip
  `Set-Cookie` for other names (2024–2025) — check sign-in on staging. Sign-out deletes the cookie.
- `lib/shop/auth.ts`: `getUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireAdmin()` call `verifySessionCookie(cookie, true)`.
- `scripts/set-admin.ts <email>` creates the user if missing, sets the claim `{ admin: true }` and
  prints a set-password link. The user signs in again to get the claim.

## Images

App Hosting has no native `next/image` optimisation (July 2026). The admin upload runs sharp on the
server: WebP at **320, 640, 960, 1280** px wide → Storage `products/<productId>/<n>-<width>.webp`
(home images: `content/home/<n>-<width>.webp`). `lib/images/loader.ts` returns the smallest width
≥ the requested one (max 1280). Images in `public/` are pre-sized WebP or AVIF. Uploads need
`experimental.serverActions.bodySizeLimit` in `next.config.ts` (the default is 1 MB).

## Env and secrets

- `apphosting.yaml`: public values with `value:`; secrets with `secret: <name>`, created with
  `firebase apphosting:secrets:set <name>`. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values need `availability: [BUILD, RUNTIME]`.
- Per-environment values: `apphosting.staging.yaml`, `apphosting.production.yaml` (the backend's
  environment name picks the file).
- Secrets: `RESEND_API_KEY`, `TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY`, `ORDER_LINK_SECRET`, the bank keys. Never in
  `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, Firestore, logs or git.

## Deploy

- Staging: backend in `<slug>-staging` (Thrio's billing), region `europe-west4`, live branch `main`,
  automatic rollouts on. Set the environment name and the secrets **before** the first rollout.
- Production: backend in `<slug>-prod` (the client's billing), automatic rollouts **off**. `/ship` runs
  `firebase apphosting:rollouts:create <backend> --git_branch main --project <slug>-prod`.
- Custom domain: add it in App Hosting, then create the records on Cloudflare as **DNS only**.
- A budget alert on both projects. Daily Firestore backups from `shop:backups`.
